+### Resource limits
+
+A container's page has a **Resources** panel: its memory limit and CPU
+limit (cores), with what it used at the last monitoring sample.
+*Change limits* (`action.updates`) changes them on the running container
+with `docker update`
+([`app/ssh/docker_resources.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/ssh/docker_resources.py)),
+without a restart:
+
+- **Memory** like `512m`, `1.5g`, `2 GiB` (at least 6 MiB). The
+  memory+swap limit is set to twice the memory, the default
+  `docker run --memory` gives, so lowering memory below an earlier swap
+  limit works. Docker can't remove a memory limit in place: recreate the
+  container for that.
+- **CPU** as cores (`0.5`, `2`); `0` removes the CPU limit.
+- **Restart policy** (`no`, `on-failure`, `always`, `unless-stopped`) and,
+  for `on-failure`, the number of retries.
+
+An empty field keeps its value. For a Compose service the compose file's
+values come back the next time the stack is recreated (the page says
+so). debcontrol's own containers are refused (audited as a refusal).
+Audited as `machine.container.resources` with the new values.
+
