+### One image: details, layers, pull, tag, remove
+
+A click on an image in the list opens its page
+(`/machines/{id}/docker/images/{image_id}`, `machine.view`), read live
+from the machine
+([`app/ssh/docker_images.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/ssh/docker_images.py)):
+tags, digests, created, size, platform, entrypoint, command, user,
+working directory, exposed ports, the containers using it, labels, and
+its **layers** (`docker history`, oldest first, each build step with its
+size). The image's environment variables are never read: they can carry
+secrets baked into an image.
+
+With `action.updates`:
+
+- **Pull** - on the Images page, any reference (`nginx:1.27`,
+  `ghcr.io/owner/app@sha256:...`); on an image's page, *Pull ... again*
+  per tag gets the newest image for that tag. A pull runs as a job (*Pull
+  image*, cancellable) whose result has the pulled image id; running
+  containers keep their image until they are updated.
+- **Tag** - `docker tag` under a new name (`registry.example.com/app:1.2.3`).
+- **Remove** - `docker image rm`, never forced: removing a tag keeps the
+  image while another tag points to it, and Docker refuses an image a
+  container uses (its answer is shown). The list offers *Remove* only for
+  images no container uses.
+
+Audited as `machine.docker.image.pull`, `.tag` and `.remove` (a failed
+remove or tag as a failure, with Docker's answer).
+
